  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a performance baseline for the multimodal approach while keeping costs low to preserve budget for exploration. Config_009 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) tests the core hypothesis that combining RNA and image modalities improves accuracy, and simultaneously probes whether multiprofile aggregation with simple avgpool pooling is beneficial. It uses the cheapest image encoder (ResNet50 vs. ViT-L), a linear RNA encoder (PCA), and simple fusion (concat), making it a low-cost experiment (expected relative cost: low, roughly 1x baseline GPU hours). This gives me a reference accuracy to compare against more expensive variants (better encoders, transformer aggregation, ViT-L) in subsequent experiments. If it performs well, I can exploit by upgrading components; if poorly, I learn that the multimodal design space needs different structural choices, reducing uncertainty about which dimensions matter most."
}

